# AEGIS Defense Control System

AEGIS is a self-contained defense dashboard with AI-style tactical intelligence, live advisory responses, edge inference simulation, and resilient control behavior. This project is designed to run as a static web app and can be deployed to GitHub Pages or any static hosting platform.

## Features

- Adaptive defense simulation
- Control mode switching: Local, Guarded, Isolated, Safe Hold
- Edge AI layer called Nexus
- Live Vigil advisory responses
- Threat monitoring and defense map model
- Scenario presets for normal, heavy attack, and network degradation

## Run locally

Open `index.html` directly in a browser, or run a local static server:

```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000
```

Then visit:

```text
http://localhost:8000
```

## Deploy to GitHub Pages

1. Push this repo to GitHub.
2. In the repository settings, open Pages.
3. Select "Deploy from a branch".
4. Choose the `main` branch and root folder `/`.
5. Save and wait for the site to build.

Your site will be available at:

```text
https://<your-username>.github.io/aegis-defense-ai/
```

## AI tech intelligence layer

The app simulates an AI-powered defense layer with:

- real-time advisory generation
- local inference prioritization
- scenario-driven risk adaptation
- defensive policy recommendations
- resilient control logic under degraded network conditions

## Files

- `index.html` — dashboard structure and UI
- `styles.css` — visual design and layout
- `app.js` — simulation and AI-style control logic

